        <mxCell id="t12" value="&lt;b&gt;Confirmed multiplicity: &lt;/b&gt;1 at the Equipment end of Booking—Equipment (FR02: “Each booking identifies exactly one equipment item”). All other association ends are unresolved and deliberately left unlabelled." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=0;fontSize=12;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="408" width="990" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n13" value="&lt;b&gt;OPEN QUESTIONS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Q1 Student–Booking &lt;/b&gt;(ask: lecturers, equipment technician) — Is every booking made by exactly one student, or can a group/class booking involve several? Can a student have zero bookings? FR01 only says a student may make more than one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Q2 Booking–Equipment &lt;/b&gt;(ask: equipment technician) — How many bookings may reference the same equipment item over time, and may their dates overlap?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Q3 Staff Member–Booking &lt;/b&gt;(ask: equipment technician, service manager) — Is each booking request reviewed by exactly one staff member, or can several review it? Must every booking be reviewed?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Q4 Staff Member–Equipment &lt;/b&gt;(ask: equipment technician, college management) — Can several staff members manage availability of the same item? Can an item have no staff member responsible?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Q5 Booking status (FR06) &lt;/b&gt;(ask: equipment technician) — How is the approve/reject decision stored: a status on Booking, or a separate review record (who, when, why)? Is a “booking request” the same thing as a “booking”?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Q6 Student details &lt;/b&gt;(ask: equipment technician, data protection representative) — Does the system need to record a student ID, name or email address? None is stated in FR01–FR06." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;spacingTop=2;fontSize=12;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="462" width="990" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
